        §5Deathcap!
§6╚════════.✵.═╝
§8Mushroom poisoning results from the ingestion or contamination of mushrooms that contain toxic substances. The symptoms can vary from slight discomfort to death within 10 days.
#- §8Amanita phalloides, commonly known as Death Cap is one such mushroom. Although toxic, it holds a striking resemblance to several edible species, making it a very sticky situation should you come face to face with one without knowing it. Speaking of 
toxic and sticky... 
#- §8Deathcap Island is the place to be! Maybe I’m biased because I’m a witch, §oand all my friends are there§0§8, but I adore this place. So much so, I’m proud to announce The Spyglass Tavern 2: The Sequel! I packed up my things, bought myself a merchant wagon and a fortune teller tent complete 
#- §8with the fortune teller, and made my way via boats and magic to the island and set up shop. Quite literally. I’m also announcing my new shop Spooky & Stinky.
A banner shop based on the name, and located in the market area where you can find other great shops. Most notable
#- §8is the bee shop with so much honey dripping from the walls that it’s a sweet tooth’s paradise or a person with melissophobia‘s nightmare. The Mushroom Village is also a thriving shopping area with many merchants. Opposite my shop, you can find the Dragon
#- §8Hotel, let’s just call it a ‘§osafe zone§0§8' for now where you can sleep soundly knowing your impending doom is just outside the window. Next to that is Soul Corp, it’s been abandoned for a while now, and I’m not entirely sure what they even did… do… did...? I was planning to sneak inside and   
#- §8find out because something feels 'off' about that place. Anyway, there’s a beautiful shield gallery with some of the most exquisite craftsmanship I’ve ever seen in the field of shield making. Nice day trip out. Then there’s the infamous /warp random who finally decided to add
#- §8doors.....lovely addition!
Deathcap also has its own bay and harbour due to a large number of visitors arriving or fleeing on boats. 
Some people say there’s a black market in the works but I’ve yet to visit... 
There’s also an airport, for the large number of visitors arriving and fleeing.
#- §8It also has its own parkland, a wonderful nature reserve for frogs and mooshrooms. 
I took the liberty of building my own witch hut to stay in nearby because §oI don’t trust anything here.§0
§8One of the things that intrigued me about this land was Links Laboratory. §2🧪
#- §8Now I know what you’re thinking: §7§owhy would a witch be interested in science, isn’t there an ongoing war between the two and to be involved with each other would be treason of the highest degree? §0§8Yes, you would be right. I believe this lab holds some vital secrets about why Craftadia
#- §8is in chaos and §6I WILL FIND OUT! §8I shall infiltrate the lab and discover its mysteries. Or… we could just work together. Link is actually a nice person (§owhen you take away the whole mad scientist vibe§0§8), so maybe I should have a meeting with them first and have a formal discussion.
#- §8Combining our skills and powers might really come in handy if we are to face §0The Darkness.

§5ₐH! yₒᵤ Sₐᵢd ᵢt ₐgₐᵢn... 
yₒᵤ kNₒw sₒmₑthᵢNg dₒN't yₒᵤ??

§8And now the main attraction! The Maze!

§5Swₑₑtpₑₐ wₐᵢt...
#- §8Most who enter never make it out, but wow it’s fun. As one of the test rabbits, I can say with certainty that it’s infuriatingly a-maze-ing and well worth a visit to test your puzzle-solving abilities. And if we never see you again, '§4management is not responsible for any loss of life or
#- §4property§8'. Oh, wait no, that was for the entire island. Try not to step on slime or touch the mushrooms and you’ll be fine. 

