§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗    §2ᴇᴍᴇʀᴀʟᴅ ᴘʀɪɴᴄᴇꜱꜱ:
        ᴘᴀʀᴛ ᴛᴡᴏ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝§2Castien the elf wouldn’t stop bombarding Fern with questions. “§cSo, is it true you’re over 200 years old? Does that mean Honey the bee is also 200 years old? How does that even work? Are you really 
#- §cmade of fern and flowers? What happens in winter or if you get dehydrated? Your mother was a witch, right? Are you truly the only one who can destroy ‘§5ɨȶ§c’? And what about §0The Darkness§c? Was that caused by…”
§2A sword unlike anything the elf had seen before was 
#- §2suddenly pressed under his chin. “Please stop with all the questions it’s getting annoying,” said Fern sternly. Castien saw her eyes glistening with tears. “§cI apologise, quite right, we must stick to the mission at hand§2”. Fern lowered the sword and used Honey as a makeshift tissue. 
#- §2“No, I’m sorry, it’s just been… 
    a long 200 years”. 

As the sun set, they finally arrived at a giant lush cave in the middle of nowhere. The elf prince had found a note placed perfectly where the Emerald Crown should have been. It read:
§5ȶɦɛ ɛռɖ ɨֆ ƈօʍɨռɢ
#- §2Along with this very location. Unnaturally Fern found herself fully trusting Castien with his every word and a little self-conscious. It’s safe to assume she had a small crush on this elf. Thankfully elves also live incredibly long lives. They entered the cave and made their
#- §2way down deeper until the bright green turned into moody grey. They walked a long time in silence, occasionally taking turns protecting each other from mobs. They reached a stone structure. “§cThis far underground can only mean one thing, it’s a Stronghold, like in the stories, must be...§2”
#- §2exclaimed Castien with excitement. Fern remained silent, her mind spinning with thoughts. They both went inside and navigated the long maze of hallways until at last, there it was. An End Portal! Not activated, but right before their eyes! Castien gave Fern a playful nudge "§cthis is  
#- §camazing, the stories where… wait, that’s my crown!§2” The elf ran over to the other side of the room where the Emerald Crown had been placed by unknown hands. It came with a second note that read: §5ֆȶɛǟʟɨռɢ ʏօʊʀ ֆȶʊքɨɖ ƈʀօառ աǟֆ ȶɦɛ օռʟʏ աǟʏ ɨ ƈօʊʟɖ ɮʀɨռɢ ʄɛʀռ ȶօ ȶɦɨֆ քօʀȶǟʟ, 
#- §5ʍʏ ǟքօʟօɢɨɛֆ, ɨȶ.

§2“§cOkay, are you going to say something now or just stare?§2” 

Fern took a deep sigh... 

“Craftadia has a way to get to the end, §5ɨȶ§2 was telling the truth after all”.
#- §2Castien rolled his eyes “§cand it took stealing my crown for you to even care§2”. Fern touched her sword again and shouted “a very long 200 years okay”. The elf took a step back and started rubbing his hands together in plotting mode. “§cWell, we know that §5ɨȶ §cwants us to activate the portal
#- §cand jump in§2”. Fern turned around and started walking away. “Yeah, a great plan, you first”. The elf threw a small pebble at Fern to momentarily stop her. “§cOi Fernie… thanks for getting the crown back at least, maybe one day, if you’re lucky, you could have one of your own”.
#- §2Fern smirked, turned back around and said “alright then...  §oCas..§2
let's§0 §2do this, what could possibly go wrong?!"
