 §9A guide for making a        house a home!
#-    §3⛏*⋆§9Article Five§3⋆*⛏
        §4ᴴᵒʷ ᵀᵒ ᴱˢᶜᵃᵖᵉ
§8-------------------
§d┏------✦❘༻༺❘✦------┓
    By MissPortinari
┗------✦❘༻༺❘✦------┛
§8-------------------§1When I was little my mother taught me that trick that we've all heard before, where you put your hand on one wall, and just follow it all the way
#- §1t§to the end! 

It works for many 2D mazes! (§ospecifically, ones where there is an entrance on one side, and an exit on the other§0§1). But since that day, I've been obsessed with the idea of designing a maze where... 
          §4**that trick 
          will NOT work** 
#- §1In this maze, there are §43 sections§1, and each one has a different way of confounding the trick.

§2✥ Section One:§9
Levels 1 and 2 are linked together, and the true path weaves up and down between them. Following the wall only leads you left or right, but you have to
#- §9go §4*DOWN* §9to make progress. 

§1{Tip: Pay attention to details and decor. If you find §4*flowering azaleas*§1, then you're on the right track. But that big cave is a §4*feeder* §1cave that will take you off the true path and back to the start again!} 
#- §2✥ Section Two: §9As you traverse the first section, you might hear the sound of pistons. This is coming from Level 3 [otherwise known as piston hell]. This section of the maze §4*changes* §9over time. Doorways open and close, and dead-ends spring to life. If you follow the wall blindly, 
#- §9Also, you have to find a §4*button room*§9 before you can use the exit... §oit's uh complicated. §0§9We take no responsibility for scrambled brains.

§1{It's a fully 2D maze, but because of the piston doors, you can't reliably follow a wall to the exit. The exist doors are also
#- §1timed. You need to 
§4*find the button room*§1, then figure out the fastest way from there to the exit, then trigger the button and run}

{Tip: Ironically, 
you can use the 
§4*follow the right wall*§1 trick to get from 
the button room 
to the exit!)  
#- §2✥ Section Three: §9This is a fully 3D section of the maze! You can't follow a wall the way you can in a 2D maze, because each wall is now a flat plane rather than a long ribbon. There are no tricks you can use here, just §4*check all the paths*§9, and make sure to §4*check up in the corners*§9 too!
#- §9You'll have to 
swim through a 
§4*1x1 opening*§9 to get out so look carefully!

§1{This section was inspired by MC Escher's "Relativity". Stand just above the conduit to see!}

§oPs: Tropical fish spawn here, so feel free to harvest them!
#- §2✥ General Advice: 

§9- Don't forget 
to look up!

- Harvest the crops and take any goodies you might find hidden in the barrels. You never know what you might find!

- You may climb on 
the top of the maze!
#- §2Go visit §5/warp maze
§2and give it a go!
§8-------------------
If this maze guide did not make anything easier, you are not alone. For more information and support please 
email us at§::

§7§nwitchmag@notaclue.com
