    §8/warp codebook
§6└───   §c⋆⋅☆⋅⋆   §6───┘
§cNow, this is a warp I wish I knew about before embarking on my book-making adventures! 

When I first began creating this magazine, I had no idea how complicated text formatting would be. 
#- §cWell, fear no longer my creative Craftadians because /warp codebook has got you covered! They provide a handy little book with all the text codes neatly displayed for you!

I'd like to talk more about the rest of the place (if I may), as 
it's very intriguing.
#- §cWhen you walk out of the small shop (that also sells water and lava buckets), you are met with a sparkling amethyst roof and a very very very deep tunnel full of stairs. It's a huge cave that's been hollowed out and has spaces for more shops I'm assuming. It is quite the sight to behold
#- §cand quite a project to undertake. I'm looking forward to seeing the final thing one day.

If you are cheeky and sneaky like me and just can't help yourself, upstairs you will find a cute living area and storage space. I love the head decorations and the storage planning is  
#- §cmuch better than mine. Good job! This place is known as Mempo's Keep... I know this because guess what... it's right next door to my land where The Spyglass Tavern #1 and my home base reside. Small world! 
{§7ps: I'm sorry it's taken so long to review your warp but see... I never forgot!§c}
#- §cAlso since I started making this issue, Mempo became a landowner on Deathcap so, please visit their ongoing project: /warp cthulu brought to you by /warp bucket...

§6┌───   §c⋆⋅☆⋅⋆   §6───┐
    §8I give this warp:
      §6★★★★★ 5.0
└───   §c⋆⋅☆⋅⋆   §6───┘
